                <pb facs="0171" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2413/141.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic">July 22,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon directs Mr. Rockhill to express to the foreign office this
                    Government’s satisfaction on learning of the deputation of T’ang Shao-yi, who
                    will be very welcome.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
